    "content": "The Masters Green Jacket is one of golf's most exclusive prizes, awarded since 1949 to the Masters champion and worn by Augusta National members since 1937 to identify them to patrons. It is an \"Augusta Green\" (Pantone 342C) wool blazer featuring an embroidered left-breast patch. Winners may take the jacket home for one year before returning it to be stored on-site.Key Facts About the Green Jacket:Storage & Usage: Winners return their jackets to the clubhouse 12 months after their victory, where they are stored in a designated cloakroom and worn only while on the premises.Multiple Winners: While winners get to keep their initial jacket for a year, if they win again, they do not get a new one, unless a new fit is needed.The \"Rule\": Only a first-time and reigning champion may remove his jacket from the Augusta National club grounds.Origin: Inspired by red jackets worn by captains at Royal Liverpool, co-founder Bobby Jones brought the concept to Augusta, with the first jackets introduced in 1937 to differentiate members from patrons.Design: Made of lightweight, wool, it is a single-breasted blazer featuring brass buttons with the PGA logo.Most Recent Champion: Rory McIlroy won the 2026 Masters, marking a consecutive win and his second Green Jacket.Did You Know?The Green Jacket is a prestigious item, and winners tend to hold it in high regard. Hideki Matsuyama won the Masters in 2021 and for the entire first year that he was allowed to keep his Green Jacket, he never once had it dry cleaned.Last Updated: April 12, 2026 The Masters Green Jacket is one of golf's most exclusive prizes, awarded since 1949 to the Masters champion and worn by Augusta National members since 1937 to identify them to patrons. It is an \"Augusta Green\" (Pantone 342C) wool blazer featuring an embroidered left-breast patch. Winners may take the jacket home for one year before returning it to be stored on-site. Key Facts About the Green Jacket: Storage & Usage: Winners return their jackets to the clubhouse 12 months after their victory, where they are stored in a designated cloakroom and worn only while on the premises. Multiple Winners: While winners get to keep their initial jacket for a year, if they win again, they do not get a new one, unless a new fit is needed. The \"Rule\": Only a first-time and reigning champion may remove his jacket from the Augusta National club grounds. Origin: Inspired by red jackets worn by captains at Royal Liverpool, co-founder Bobby Jones brought the concept to Augusta, with the first jackets introduced in 1937 to differentiate members from patrons. Design: Made of lightweight, wool, it is a single-breasted blazer featuring brass buttons with the PGA logo. Most Recent Champion: Rory McIlroy won the 2026 Masters, marking a consecutive win and his second Green Jacket. Did You Know?The Green Jacket is a prestigious item, and winners tend to hold it in high regard. Hideki Matsuyama won the Masters in 2021 and for the entire first year that he was allowed to keep his Green Jacket, he never once had it dry cleaned. Last Updated: April 12, 2026",
